---

## Test Smell Audit — `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 · .NET 10 · Integration test class (`[TestCategory("Integration")]`)
**Taxonomy:** [testsmells.org](https://testsmells.org/) 19-smell academic catalog (Peruma et al., ESEC/FSE 2020)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 2 | 2 |
| Medium | 2 | 2 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **4** | **4** |

*4 of 8 test methods have at least one smell. The remaining 4 are clean.*

---

### Findings by Severity

#### ❶ Conditional Test Logic — **High**

**Academic name:** Conditional Test Logic
**Affected test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 95)
**Why High:** Control flow inside a test hides paths that may never execute, regardless of integration scope. This smell is not downgraded for integration tests.

```csharp
// SMELL: the if/else means one branch is never tested
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix — split into two explicit tests:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscountRate()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsInstanceOfType<PremiumUser>(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** One branch is dead code in every run — you have invisible coverage and the assertion that *should* fire never does.

---

#### ❷ Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — **High**

**Academic name:** Unknown Test / Empty Test
**Affected test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
// SMELL: no assertion — passes even if every insert silently fails
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Fix — assert the observable effect:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count, "All 100 bulk-inserted users should be persisted.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** This test gives false confidence — it inflates pass counts and coverage metrics while verifying nothing.

---

#### ❸ Sleepy Test — **Medium** *(downgraded from High — integration calibration)*

**Academic name:** Sleepy Test
**Affected test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
// SMELL: Thread.Sleep blocks for 3 seconds; also blocking call in async method
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    Thread.Sleep(3000);   // ← hard 3-second wait

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
}
```

**Why Medium, not High:** The class is `[TestCategory("Integration")]`, so async coordination delays are expected. However, `Thread.Sleep` (blocking a thread-pool thread inside an `async` method) is still poor practice. Use a polling loop or `Task.Delay` with a timeout.

**Fix — poll with timeout:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(5);
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
            break;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        "Notification should be sent within 5 seconds of insert.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Adds 3 seconds of unconditional wall-clock time to every suite run and introduces non-deterministic failures on slow machines.

---

#### ❹ Assertion Roulette — **Medium**

**Academic name:** Assertion Roulette
**Affected test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
// SMELL: 4 assertions, none with a message — which one failed?
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix — add assertion messages:**

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "Inserted user should be retrievable by email.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip through persistence.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip through persistence.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Persisted user should have a positive auto-generated ID.");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** When a failure occurs in CI, the stack trace says `Assert.AreEqual failed` with no context. Developers waste time re-reading the test to identify which property was wrong.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

These 4 tests are well-designed — clean arrange/act/assert, no smells:

| Test | Notes |
|------|-------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear single behavior, 2 focused assertions |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Clean negative check with `Assert.IsNull` |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | `Assert.AreEqual(3, …)` is contextually obvious (3 items just inserted) — not Magic Number |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Good concurrency test with proper `await` and count verification |

---

### Smells Not Detected (15 of 19)

| Smell | Status |
|-------|--------|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean — uses in-memory SQLite, no real external resources |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean — all tests call ≤3 distinct production methods |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean — count literals (3, 10, 100) are contextually self-documenting |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean — no `.ToString()` comparisons |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean — no `try`/`catch` blocks |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean — `_connection` and `_repository` used by all 8 tests |
| Ignored/Disabled Test | ✅ Clean — no `[Ignore]` or `Skip` |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean — no duplicated assertion statements |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean — tests target distinct behaviors |
| Constructor Initialization | ✅ Clean — uses `[TestInitialize]`, not constructor |
| Default Test | ✅ Clean — class is properly named |
| Redundant Print | ✅ Clean — no `Console.WriteLine` |
| Redundant Assertion | ✅ Clean — no tautological assertions |
| Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean — in-memory DB created in setup |
| Empty Test | ✅ Clean — no completely empty methods |

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | **Assertion-Free Test** (`BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors`) | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, …)` after the loop | ~1 min |
| 2 | **Conditional Test Logic** (`GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType`) | Split into two tests with explicit type setup | ~5 min |
